---
id: DD-002
type: rule
family: deferred-debt
title: HACK comment without tracking reference
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 1

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs, .py, .go, .rs]
allowlist: []

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '//\s*(HACK|XXX)\b(?!.*([A-Z]+-\d+|#\d+|issue|ticket))'

related: [DD-001]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

This code is explicitly marked as a hack with no plan for remediation.
Labeling code as a hack without a tracking artifact turns the label
into permission to leave it indefinitely.

Create a ticket documenting why the hack exists, what the proper
solution looks like, and what blocks it. Reference it in the comment:
`// HACK(PROJ-789): workaround for upstream bug, fix when v3 ships`.
